It should work for any 64-bit unix-based box, however, Hearse support
is limited to 'official releases'. Anyone who wants to compile their
own needs to make sure the version stamp of the bones files produced
are the same, ie needs to compile with the same game options (eg
compression on or off, mail daemon enabled or disabled, etc).  Nethack
is rather unforgiving of differences in this regard and will refuse to
load such bones files, so Hearse rejects them as incompatible.

If anyone runs into a unix distribution where the 'out of the box' 64-
bit Nethack doesn't produce bones files that can be uploaded to
Hearse, please let me know.

